# Syllabus Version 1: 

## Phase 1: Foundations

Lesson 1: What makes a prompt “engineered” (role, context, constraints).

Lesson 2: Experimenting — casual vs engineered prompts.

Lesson 3: Structuring prompts (templates, formatting, step-by-step instructions).

## Phase 2: Techniques

Lesson 4: Few-shot prompting (examples).

Lesson 5: Chain of thought (step-by-step reasoning).

Lesson 6: Advanced structures (system + user prompts, multi-turn workflows).

## Phase 3: Workflows

Lesson 7: Building a prompt workflow (inputs, templates, outputs).

Lesson 8: Real-world mini project (choose a use case like blog drafting or summarization assistant).

## Phase 4: Beyond Prompting

Lesson 9: Evaluation (testing prompts systematically).

Lesson 10: Integration (embedding prompts into apps, APIs, and automation).

Lesson 11: Best practices + your blog publishing plan.


# Version 2: Developer-Oriented Prompt Engineering Syllabus


## Phase 1: Foundations (Prompt Basics)

Prompt Engineering vs. Casual Use

Roles, context, constraints.

Hands-on: casual vs engineered prompts (experimenting in chat).

Prompt Templates & Structures

Placeholders, parameterization.

Hands-on: design a reusable summarization template.

Controlling Output

Formatting, style, tone, length.

Hands-on: generate structured JSON responses for downstream use.

## Phase 2: Advanced Prompting Techniques

Few-Shot Prompting

Using examples to guide the model.

Hands-on: sentiment classifier with few-shot examples.

Chain-of-Thought Prompting

For reasoning tasks.

Hands-on: step-by-step math/logic prompts.

Multi-Turn Workflows

Breaking tasks into steps across prompts.

Hands-on: design a mini Q&A assistant with follow-up refinement.

## Phase 3: Workflows & Deployment

Designing Prompt Workflows

Input capture → prompt template → response → post-processing.

Hands-on: build a workflow that turns meeting notes into action items.

APIs & Programmatic Use

OpenAI API basics, LangChain, LlamaIndex, or direct scripting.

Hands-on: call an API with a prompt template in Python.

Prompt Libraries & Modularity

Organizing reusable prompts.

Hands-on: build a small “prompt toolkit” for text analysis tasks.

## Phase 4: Evaluations & Integrations

Prompt Evaluation

Measuring consistency, accuracy, robustness.

Hands-on: run A/B tests on two prompt versions.

Integration into Systems

Connecting to pipelines, apps, or workflows.

Hands-on: integrate a prompt workflow into a data science pipeline (e.g., automated report generation).

Best Practices & Maintenance

Avoiding pitfalls, documenting prompts, versioning.

Hands-on: write a “prompt spec” for one of your workflows.

## Phase 5: Capstone

Mini Project (Capstone)

Choose one:

A text analysis pipeline (summarization, classification, insight extraction).

A developer tool (docstring generator, code reviewer, query explainer).

A workflow assistant (turn raw data into polished insights).

Deliverable: A working prototype + blog post documenting it.